cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "It from Bit via Gödel"
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite the repository using the metadata
  below. Once a preprint exists, cite that in preference and use the
  repository DOI for the exact source state it was built from.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Small
    given-names: John
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7123-411X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JohnSmall/it-from-bit-2026"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A multi-paper series deriving Standard Model structure, the quantum
  postulates, and spacetime dimensionality from self-reference and
  computability. Paper 1 covers foundations; Paper 2 derives spacetime from
  the FANOUT boundary. The repository holds the LaTeX sources, the Zotero
  exported bibliographies, the supporting computations, and an archive of the
  research conversations from which the work developed.
keywords:
  - quantum foundations
  - self-reference
  - negative probability
  - Hopf fibration
  - division algebras
  - Standard Model
  - computability
